  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. Past tickets ask for a timer or schedule to shut down or sleep a PC after a set duration. #34919 and #32852 were closed as duplicates of #28490, which is the main ticket for a scheduled shutdown/sleep utility. #39282 and #17970 were closed in favour of the same request. PowerToys has no such tool yet, so add your vote to #28490. In the meantime you can use the built-in Windows command. Press Win+R and run `shutdown /s /t N`, where N is the number of seconds. For example, `shutdown /s /t 3600` shuts down after 60 minutes, and `shutdown /a` cancels it. Running `shutdown /i` opens a graphical dialog. You can also make a shortcut to shutdown.exe, or use Task Scheduler to trigger it. Sleep has no equivalent built-in command, so it needs a script or a third-party tool."
 },
